# Images

<h2 id="wg-082">Write alternative text for meaningful images</h2>

Describe what the image shows that the person needs. Leave the alternative text empty for a decorative image. Do not start with “image of”.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| alt="floorplan.png" | alt="Ground floor: kitchen at the back, lounge at the front, hall in the middle." |
| alt="Image of a camera snapshot" | alt="Front door camera at 18:42: a delivery driver at the door holding a parcel." |
| alt="Light bulb icon" on a button already labelled Turn on | alt="" (the button text already says it) |

If the image carries information, put the same information in text too. Do not put text inside an image if you can write it as text.

## Charts, floor plans and snapshots

Give a chart a table or a sentence with the same facts. See [Charts and data](charts-and-data.html). Say when a camera picture is old.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| The label “Live” on a snapshot taken 9 minutes ago. | Snapshot from 09:06. Select **Refresh** to get a new one. |
